# Kiosk lock (PR #19, battery prompt added in #21)

## Decisions (user chose, Oct 2026)

- Full lock task when the app is device owner; plain `startLockTask()` (screen pinning) otherwise.
- Controlled from Home Assistant: screen settings `kiosk` (switch "Kiosk lock") and `kioskPin` (text "Kiosk PIN", password mode, 4–8 digits, `ScreenSettings.KIOSK_PIN`; invalid PINs are dropped in `validated()`).
- Enrollment: QR code from the editor first (Screens → Tablets → Enroll a tablet), `scripts/enroll-device-owner.sh` (ported from RPI, keeps `--fresh` and `DELETE_FAILED_APP_PINNED`) as the fallback.
- Names and patterns follow RPI (`~/StudioProjects/RPI/.cursor/rules/kiosk-lock-task-context.mdc`): `KioskManager`, `LockTaskDeviceAdminReceiver`, `relaunchKioskIfUnlocked(reason)`, persisted suppress flag. Here `KioskManager` is a Hilt `@Singleton`, not an `object`.

## Player

- `KioskManager`: `KioskState { OFF, PINNED, LOCKED }` from `lockTaskModeState`; device-owner policies (lock task packages + `LOCK_TASK_FEATURE_GLOBAL_ACTIONS` on API 28+, persistent HOME, status bar + keyguard disabled, `DISALLOW_SAFE_BOOT/FACTORY_RESET/ADD_USER`), each reversible; `SecurityException` logged "Is this app a device owner?". `removeDeviceOwner()` clears policies + `clearDeviceOwnerApp`.
- Two device admins on purpose: `LockTaskDeviceAdminReceiver` (device owner) and the older `ScreenOffAdminReceiver`, so existing screen-off activations survive. `ScreenPowerRepository.canTurnScreenOff()` accepts either.
- `PlayerPreferencesRepository`: `kiosk_enabled` and `kiosk_suppressed` (local unlock, survives restarts). Turning `kiosk_enabled` false → true clears the suppress flag.
- `ViewState.isKioskEnabled` is `Boolean?` (null until DataStore is read) so lock task isn't stopped and restarted at startup. `isKioskWanted = isKioskEnabled && !isLocallyUnlocked`.
- `MainActivity.observeKiosk` collects `isKioskWanted` under `repeatOnLifecycle(RESUMED)` → re-pins after the user unpins, and after the battery dialog closes.
- PIN: settings (long press top bar) shows `KioskPinDialog` when kiosk wanted and a PIN is set. Right PIN → settings with "Unlock tablet"; while unlocked "Lock again". No PIN → no local unlock. "Stop managing this tablet" only while unlocked. Self-start / screen-off / battery buttons hidden while locked (lock task blocks those system screens).
- Updates while only pinned: `PlayerEvent.StopScreenPinning` before the install confirmation; resume re-pins.
- `DeviceState.kiosk` reports `off`/`pinned`/`locked` → HA `binary_sensor` attribute and the editor's tablet list icon.

## QR enrollment

- Player: `ProvisioningModeActivity` (`GET_PROVISIONING_MODE` → fully managed) and `PolicyComplianceActivity` (`ADMIN_POLICY_COMPLIANCE` → `KioskManager.onProvisioned`, `RESULT_OK`); receiver's `onProfileProvisioningComplete` for older Android. `onProvisioned` reads admin extra `server`, enables kiosk.
- Server `EnrollmentService`: tokens reusable for 60 min (deviation from the plan's single use — several tablets per code, download retries); provisioning JSON with admin component, `http://<host>:8100/player/apk?enroll=<token>`, signature checksum (falls back to the APK's package checksum), skip encryption, leave system apps, optional Wi-Fi, admin extras `{server}`. `POST /api/enrollment` (409 when no APK or host).
- `tools/package_addon.sh` writes `signatureChecksum` (SHA-256 of the signing cert, URL-safe Base64, no padding) to `version.json` via `apksigner` (needs Java: Android Studio's jbr).
- A QR-enrolled tablet starts locked and stays locked until paired; then it follows its screen's Kiosk lock (default off → turn it on before pairing).

## Gotchas

- The app ID changed in #20 (`dev.remotescreens.player` → `tech.shaffersoftworks.remotescreens.player`): a different app, so device-owner tablets need a factory reset and re-enrollment. The admin component string lives in `EnrollmentService` and the adb script.
- The PIN is plain text in HA state/history and on the LAN WebSocket — a deterrent, not security.
- Tablets are only offered an APK with a higher versionCode; same-version deploys don't reach them.

## Not verified

Nothing has been tested on a real tablet yet: QR provisioning on a factory-reset device, lock task policies, pin/unpin recovery, PIN flow, update install while pinned, removal.
